0.4.0: camera/film vocabulary, film library, canonical defaults

CLI renamed to match the architecture: -c/--camera selects the
format/process archetype (optics, grain, flash, framing, age),
-f/--film the color chemistry. 0.3.x -p/--preset/--lut remain as
quiet aliases.

Films are now named, not pathed: -f matches against the film library
(data/luts, or $POLAJUICE_FILMS) by exact stem, then case-insensitive
substring; ambiguity lists candidates. Each camera declares a
canonical film applied automatically when installed, falling back to
the built-in scalar engine with a note; --no-film forces scalars.
New 'films [filter]' subcommand lists installed stocks; 'cameras'
shows each archetype with its default film.

Makefile: auto header dependencies via -MMD (editing internal.h
previously left stale objects with a mismatched struct layout);
portable install target (BSD install has no -D). New
scripts/release.sh automates import-build-test-commit-tag-push with
preflight checks that refuse non-fast-forward states and existing
tags.
